ggml-cpu repack: dynamic chunks for MoE MUL_MAT_ID (on top of 0001)

Upstream splits every expert's columns statically (ith*ne01/nth), so the op lasts as long as the slowest thread. On a
Pixel 10 the threads run on a big core and on medium cores in two clock domains. This hands out chunks of whole
NB_COLS groups over all used experts (about 4 per thread) through the threadpool chunk counter, like the dense path.
Each output column is still computed by one thread with the same kernel, so results should not change.
Correctness: arm64 under QEMU (0001-0008 plus a first 0009 that never ran, MiniCPM5 and Ling, 256 tokens): KL divergence against stock at the
tool's floor (max 3.7e-5, same top token 100%). Phone speed: not measured yet.

